  "trail_id": "01M1JF1XD7TJQWST4VANFBRAND",
  "url": "https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/146",
  "branch": "fix117",
  "base": "main",
  "title": "fix(cli): refuse hard-linked targets before writing; stop rejecting a directory merely spelled like the git directory",
  "body": "Problem\ninit-agents checked for unsafe hard links only while writing each managed target. If AGENTS.md was hard-linked to .git/config or another unaccounted file, the command could create or replace .entire/graph-agent.md before refusing, leaving a partial installation.\nThe path guard also rejected a legitimate .GIT/rules.md directory on case-sensitive filesystems even when .GIT was an ordinary directory rather than the repository administrative directory.\nSolution\nPreflight shared-inode safety for .entire/graph-agent.md, AGENTS.md, and CLAUDE.md before any managed write or success output.\nReuse handle-based inode accounting. AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md may intentionally share an inode; guide-to-instruction collisions and every unaccounted hard link remain rejected.\nKeep the write-time handle check so a target swapped after preflight is still refused before truncation.\nContinue rejecting the real Git administrative directory, while allowing a case-variant component such as .GIT when it does not resolve to that directory.\nSafety invariants\nUnsafe hard links fail before any managed file is created, replaced, or reported as written.\nExisting guide content, Git configuration, and external hard-linked files remain unchanged on refusal.\nMissing guide or instruction files are not left behind after preflight refusal.\nContainment, regular-file validation, Git-directory detection, managed-target collision checks, and write-time race protection remain enforced.\nVerification\nTests cover hard links to both .git/config and an ordinary external file, missing and existing guide cases, no partial output or files, unchanged victims, and a legitimate case-sensitive .GIT directory whose writes must not touch the real Git config. Existing topology, containment, and write-time hard-link tests remain in the suite. GitHub build, lint, and test checks are green across supported platforms.\nNon-goals\nThis change does not enumerate every inode alias or classify unaccounted links as harmless; it fails closed and recommends symlinks for sharing. It does not weaken protection for actual Git administrative directories or claim to eliminate races from an actor with filesystem rename authority.",
